# Round 62 — integrable systems deep dive: reality of roots needs what is missing

| item | obstacle | verdict |
|------|----------|---------|
| ODE/IM (Dorey–Tateo, BLZ) | no ODE whose spectral determinant is Ξ; T-Q relations do not force real roots | DEAD |
| França–LeClair 2015 equations | built for on-line zeros; uniqueness unproved | CIRCULAR |
| Baxter Q-operator, quantum Wronskian | Wronskians do not force real roots | DEAD |
| TBA / Y-systems | no kernel carrying Euler-product data | DEAD |
| Sklyanin SoV, Gaudin | Hermitian Bethe models still have complex strings | DEAD |
| Riemann–Hilbert / Painlevé | statistical, not ξ itself; a reality-preserving tau function ≡ RH | CIRCULAR |
| KdV/Toda isospectral flows | preserve but do not create real spectrum | DEAD |
| XXZ/XXX thermodynamic limits | lose prime data | DEAD |

Integrable structure gives functional relations; reality of roots always comes from a separate
self-adjointness, which is the Hilbert–Pólya problem again.
